       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: center;
       width: 100%;
       height: 100%;
   }
   ```

This way the `<button>` is just a block-level element (no longer relied upon for flex centering), and the inner `<span>` handles the vertical centering — which works consistently across all browsers including Firefox on Android.

